<title>USA: U.S. NAPM index 50.2 in Oct versus 51.7 in Sept.</title>
<headline>U.S. NAPM index 50.2 in Oct versus 51.7 in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>TEMPE, Ariz. 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Purchasing Management (NAPM) said on Friday its index of manufacturing activity fell to 50.2 in October from 51.7 in September. A listing of the main NAPM components follows:  </p>
<p>		    Oct  Sept  Aug   July  June  May  April  March</p>
<p>PMI		50.2  51.7  52.6  50.2  54.3  49.3  50.1  46.9</p>
<p>Production     56.6  54.1  57.0  52.4  55.4  52.7  52.1  46.6</p>
<p>New Orders     51.6  56.3  55.6  54.0  61.3  52.4  53.8  49.7</p>
<p>Supplier Deliv 50.7  49.7  52.5  50.9  53.2  50.0  49.2  49.9</p>
<p>Inventories    38.9  44.8  41.6  41.2  42.3  38.3  44.6  38.8</p>
<p>Employment     45.5  46.9  48.2  45.5  49.4  45.5  45.3  44.7</p>
<p>Prices	   47.1  51.2  47.4  44.5  49.0  50.8  40.1  39.5</p>
<p>Export Orders  56.1  56.8  57.2  53.8  53.9  56.9  51.4  50.4</p>
<p>Imports	  53.8  51.8  50.6  53.7  48.6  49.8  46.2  46.3</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
